      "id": 13432,
      "name": "MarioFanaticXV",
      "username": "MarioFanaticXV",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mariofanaticxv/{size}/2129_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-08-14T11:55:31.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I haven't done a big, epic RPG in a while; I tried Deus Ex: The Fall, and was sorely disappointed to find it was just part of an episodic game that was never finished, and that just didn't scratch the itch. So help me clear out my backlog by choosing one for me to go back and play through. My top choices are the moment are as follows:</p>\n<p><span class=\"bbcode-b\">Genesis</span><br>Shining Force<br>Landstalker</p>\n<p><span class=\"bbcode-b\">PS1</span><br>Vagrant Story<br>Wild Arms</p>\n<p><span class=\"bbcode-b\">DS</span><br>Mega Man: Battle Network 5 Double Team</p>\n<p><span class=\"bbcode-b\">3DS</span><br>Bravely Default</p>\n<p><span class=\"bbcode-b\">PSP</span><br>Final Fantasy IV: The After Years<br>Knights in the Nightmare</p>\n<p><span class=\"bbcode-b\">GameCube</span><br>Baten Kaitos: Eternal Wings and the Lost Ocean</p>\n<p><span class=\"bbcode-b\">Wii</span><br>Opoona</p>\n<p><span class=\"bbcode-b\">PC</span><br>Alpha Protocol<br>Quest for Glory: So You Want to be a Hero?<br>Fallout 2<br>Neverwinter Nights: Shadows of Undrentide<br>Neverwinter Nights 2: Storm of Zehir<br>Geneforge 2<br>Beyond Divinity</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:45:14.110Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
