      "created_at": "2015-08-14T16:57:09.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Craig\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/craig/48/2150_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Craig:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I refuse to play a game that forces me to create a game inside of it on my own in order to have fun. I'll stick to playing actual games.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p><br><br>This is why I avoid sandbox games; I like having an actual goal in mind. I love having multiple ways to accomplish a goal, but the idea of having no real goal at all makes it pointless to me.<br><br>Anyways, I think I'll go ahead with Shining Force; it gives me an excuse to dust off my Nomad.</p>",
